  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "overview",
      "title": "Model overview and intended purpose",
      "status": "available",
      "source": "llm_draft",
      "text": "Legacy R Logistic Regression (legacy-r-logistic) estimates the probability that a credit-card customer defaults next month and is described as being used in credit decisions; it is recorded as risk tier 1. The business purpose, target variable, input features, preprocessing steps and train fraction were inferred rather than formally documented. The model owner, developer, approval history and formal decision context are not documented. The supplied dataset is the UCI Default of Credit Card Clients data (30,000 records, Taiwan, April to September 2005), labelled as public demonstration data only and not representative of a UK bank's current portfolio.",
      "rows": []
    },
    {
