    {
      "key": "methodology",
      "title": "Algorithm and methodology",
      "status": "available",
      "source": "llm_draft",
      "text": "The model is a logistic regression fitted in R using glm with a binomial family and logit link, predicting a binary target derived from default.payment.next.month. Predictors are all training-file columns except row_id, target, SEX, AGE and ID, which yields 21 features (LIMIT_BAL, EDUCATION, MARRIAGE, PAY_0 and PAY_2 to PAY_6, BILL_AMT1 to BILL_AMT6, PAY_AMT1 to PAY_AMT6). Upstream Python code performs a stratified 80/20 train/test split (random_state default 42), drops the ID column and rows with missing values, and classifies using a hard-coded 0.35 threshold. Reported test results include ROC AUC of about 0.707, accuracy of about 0.807, precision of about 0.592 and recall of about 0.412, and R predictions matched a statsmodels reproduction within the 1e-05 tolerance. These results are not, by themselves, evidence of validation or approval.",
      "rows": []
    },
