      "source": "llm_draft",
      "text": "Categorical-coded variables (EDUCATION, MARRIAGE, PAY_x status codes) are entered as linear numeric terms, and the script applies no regularization, scaling, missing-value handling or treatment of the highly correlated BILL_AMT/PAY columns. It also assumes the log-odds of default are linear in the predictors. The 0.35 threshold has no documented rationale or cost analysis, and the feature set depends on the input file columns (a demo dataset yields only 3 features). The fitted model object is not persisted, and the production data source, data period, coefficient estimates, R/package versions and monitoring plan are not documented. Fairness metrics show an age-group disparate impact of about 0.766 and a sex disparate impact of about 0.902, but no formal fairness assessment by SEX and age band is documented.",
